# Testing Standards

## Scope and Goals
- Cover utilities, hooks, components, pages, and API routes with the right test type.
- Centralize helpers/mocks for consistent, maintainable tests.
- Enforce coverage and testing conventions.

## Test Types
- Unit (utilities, pure functions)
- Integration (hooks, API handlers with inputs/outputs)
- Component (React Testing Library; behavior-first)
- E2E (Playwright; critical user flows)

## Conventions
- Naming: `*.test.ts(x)` only.
- RTL: Prefer queries by role/text over test-ids.
- Mocks: Use MSW for HTTP. Avoid manual `fetch` mocks.
- Logging: No `console.*`. Logger is silent in tests.
- Accessibility: Provide optional `axe` helper for critical screens.

## Coverage Thresholds (Jest)
```
statements: 80
branches: 70
functions: 80
lines: 80
```

## Writing Rules
- Utilities: test happy path, edge cases, error branches.
- Hooks: test observable behavior via providers; avoid implementation details.
- Components: assert visible output/interactions; avoid class/style assertions.
- Pages: test navigation and key elements via router helpers.
- API Routes: assert `ApiResponse<T>` shape and correct status codes.
- New feature PRs must include appropriate tests.

## Building/Running Rules
- Local quick run: `yarn test:watch`.
- Full gate: `yarn check && yarn test`.
- CI: `yarn test:ci` (coverage enforced).
- E2E: `yarn test:e2e` (headless) or `yarn test:e2e:headed` (debug).
- Snapshots: update only via `yarn test:update` with justification.

## Linting
- Use `eslint-plugin-jest` and `eslint-plugin-testing-library`.
- Disallow committed `.only`/`.skip`.
- Prefer `findBy*` for async UI.

## Structure
```
src/test/
  setup/jest.setup.ts
  mocks/{handlers.ts, server.ts}
  utils/{render.tsx, next.ts, auth.ts}
tests/e2e/** (Playwright)
```

## Examples
- API handler test imports the handler, builds `NextRequest`, asserts `ApiResponse`.
- Component test uses shared `render` with providers and `userEvent`.
